      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MAD MONDAY (7) had to work very hard in the Golden Nugget last start so was far from disgraced in fading to finish midfield. He was terrific in winning his other two starts this time in, both at this circuit and distance including the 4YO Classic so deserves another chance. PINSEEKER NZ (8) makes his first appearance for Michael Young having switched from NSW since he last raced in June. He is a strong fresh performer with two wins and two placings from four attempts and should be ready to go off two trial wins. ULTIMATE MIKI (1) has been racing well from wide barriers, leading to win here two back before racing three wide without cover when fourth last week. Should get better favours from the ace draw. CYCLONE JORDY NZ (9) draws wide but came from this barrier for an eye-catching fourth in the Golden Nugget two back and has won eight of 10 tries at this circuit and distance.",
